														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4016305">
									

<p>I definitely end in an upvote, but this one is a little bit hard to follow. I know it should be easy to visualize, but it's hard to remember what they're giving up and what they are receiving. I feel like one side of the balance should be dedicated to what is being given up, and one be dedicated to what is being received. It would make things easier. The explanation for how it chooses what memories to exchange was also really difficult to follow? I now get that weight affects &quot;importance&quot;, and so does sentimental value, but the former I only got once I reached the testing logs. Also, the interview with the D-Class seems irrelevant. Other than that, I mean, I did like this. I just think it is confusing in a bad way &#8212; a &quot;huh?&quot; way instead of a &quot;<em>what??</em>&quot; way.</p>

							</div>

								
					
